/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  F23b -- Hagen-Poiseuille wedge.  FIXED iteration count, NO residualControl:
  the run goes to endTime so the grader's Class C plateau series is sampled
  uniformly.  Changed from F23 in EXACTLY TWO FIELDS (pre-registration 5.3):

      endTime         400      (was 4000)
      writeInterval   10       (was 100)

  THE CHECKPOINT COUNT IS 40, BYTE-FOR-BYTE F23's, AND THE CLASS C WINDOW STAYS
  12 CHECKPOINTS.  F17c section 8.4's warning is that changing `writeInterval`
  silently changes a criterion defined in checkpoints, so the count and the
  window are held fixed and the SPAN is registered explicitly: 12 checkpoints =
  120 iterations (F23: 1,200).

  `endTime` is the ONE MOVABLE INPUT of this registration (section 5.5).  If
  ARM-P accepts at 80 < n <= 400 the branch rule sets N_ITER = max(400, 40 x
  ceil(5n/40)) and build_f23b.py rewrites BOTH fields IN THE DESTINATION COPY,
  with the substitution asserted; this frozen source is never edited.  The
  derived writeInterval = N_ITER/40 keeps the checkpoint count at exactly 40.

  Everything else is unchanged from F23: purgeWrite 0, writeFormat ascii,
  writePrecision 12, timePrecision 6, runTimeModifiable false, no
  residualControl.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object controlDict; }

application     simpleFoam;
startFrom       startTime;
startTime       0;
stopAt          endTime;
endTime         400;           // N_ITER; must equal exact_f23b.N_ITER unless section 5.5 moved it
deltaT          1;
writeControl    timeStep;
writeInterval   10;            // = N_ITER / 40; 40 checkpoints -> the Class C plateau series
purgeWrite      0;
writeFormat     ascii;
writePrecision  12;
writeCompression off;
timeFormat      general;
timePrecision   6;
runTimeModifiable false;
